# Cursor model usage

This project uses ECC, but we are in **Cursor**, not Claude Code.

## Reviewers still auto-run

Keep the ECC loop: after writing or changing code, launch the usual reviewers (`code-reviewer`, and language reviewers when they apply). Do TDD and planning the same way.

## Always use the included / free pool

When launching **any** Task/subagent, set `model` to one of:

- `cursor-grok-4.6-high-fast`
- `composer-2.5-fast`

Never omit `model`. Never use `inherit` — Cursor remapped inherit to Claude Sonnet and billed Other Models.

Never pass Claude, Sonnet, Opus, Haiku, GPT, or Gemini unless the user explicitly names that model.

Ignore ECC frontmatter `model: sonnet` / `opus` / `haiku`.

`npm test` is local Node. It does not use any LLM.
